WEBVTT

00:01.670 --> 00:03.420
<i>Against all odds,
the Earth team</i>

00:03.590 --> 00:05.840
<i>has reached the second half
of the preselections.</i>

00:07.670 --> 00:11.010
Congratulations, proud pilots.

00:13.560 --> 00:15.180
<i>In the first race
of the playoffs,</i>

00:15.350 --> 00:18.100
<i>we had a tough pick,
Colonel Toros.</i>

00:18.600 --> 00:21.060
<i>We showed signs of progress,</i>

00:21.520 --> 00:24.400
<i>but now we've entered
a whole new league.</i>

00:26.320 --> 00:30.490
<i>I believe Molly and Jordan
have finally reached their limit.</i>

01:32.800 --> 01:35.970
I hope your team fares
better than it did against the Crogs.

01:37.010 --> 01:40.230
A second loss would put us
in a very difficult situation.

01:41.230 --> 01:44.480
I'm absolutely confident
our new strategy will pull us through.

01:46.320 --> 01:49.740
The Ultimate Prize must not fall
into the wrong hands, Don Wei.

01:50.190 --> 01:52.650
You've made that
very clear, Mr. President.

01:52.820 --> 01:54.660
We will win this race, sir.

01:54.820 --> 01:56.240
At all costs.

02:51.670 --> 02:53.720
Eva, get it together.

02:53.880 --> 02:55.300
You know you can't give up now.

02:55.760 --> 02:58.100
Just show your father
who you really are.

03:17.860 --> 03:18.990
Prince Aikka?

03:36.470 --> 03:40.180
<i>Unsaka'|', nourama tera ubarafl.!</i>

04:01.450 --> 04:03.120
Target practice?

04:03.870 --> 04:05.540
Maybe you should stand closer.

04:06.830 --> 04:10.080
My next adversary is you.

04:15.590 --> 04:16.840
Prince Aikka.

04:34.690 --> 04:36.070
Prince, wait!

04:36.360 --> 04:38.990
We were bound to race
each other sooner or later.

04:39.150 --> 04:41.360
I have received orders
from the Nourasian court.

04:41.660 --> 04:44.330
In fact, direct orders
from my father.

04:44.490 --> 04:46.500
After the start of the race,
I am to...

04:47.500 --> 04:48.500
eliminate you.

04:50.420 --> 04:51.960
You can't do that.

04:52.500 --> 04:54.380
It's against the rules.

04:54.710 --> 04:57.800
The rules forbid me
to intentionally take your life.

04:57.960 --> 04:59.760
Short of that, I am free to use

04:59.930 --> 05:02.510
any means
at my disposal to stop you.

05:03.430 --> 05:05.970
So you're going to use me
for target practice?

05:06.470 --> 05:09.390
G'dar, my mount,
was hurt during the last race.

05:09.560 --> 05:12.350
We can no longer take any chances
against your laser cannons.

05:15.690 --> 05:17.690
I was looking forward to our race.

05:18.150 --> 05:20.610
At least with you,
I didn't expect a battle.

05:20.990 --> 05:23.950
This is not the way
of the Nourasian Knights.

05:24.120 --> 05:26.410
We have always been
a peaceful people.

05:26.580 --> 05:27.950
I am truly sorry.

05:38.960 --> 05:42.720
You expect me to believe
this Nourasian Knights nonsense?

05:44.890 --> 05:46.100
Pardon me.

05:46.260 --> 05:48.390
If you're so concerned
about my cannons,

05:48.810 --> 05:51.140
we could have a clean race.

05:51.350 --> 05:52.520
A clean race?

05:52.770 --> 05:53.810
Yeah. No weapons.

05:53.980 --> 05:55.270
A race for speed.

05:55.810 --> 05:57.270
Unless you're afraid to find out

05:57.440 --> 05:59.070
which one of us
is really the best pilot.

06:07.030 --> 06:08.950
You speak like a true Nourasian.

06:12.790 --> 06:14.210
I like your offer,

06:14.370 --> 06:17.000
though I may risk
banishment from my court.

06:17.750 --> 06:20.170
If you can convince your team
to hold its fire,

06:20.340 --> 06:21.840
I promise not to use my arrows.

06:22.840 --> 06:25.340
Oh, really?
I mean, excellent.

06:25.680 --> 06:28.390
Prince, prepare yourself
to lose with honor.

06:28.810 --> 06:31.730
I am always prepared
to lose with honor, Molly.

06:31.890 --> 06:33.690
You should be prepared
to do the same.

06:47.280 --> 06:50.120
You'll never guess who
we're racing against today, Molly.

06:50.290 --> 06:51.410
Prince Aikka.

06:51.620 --> 06:53.160
Well, yeah.
How did you know?

06:53.960 --> 06:57.040
I just made a deal with the prince.
No weapons allowed.

06:57.750 --> 06:58.540
What?

06:58.790 --> 07:00.670
It'll be a clean race for speed,

07:00.840 --> 07:02.130
and no one will get hurt.

07:02.800 --> 07:04.590
It's a good thing
I got a book in the turret.

07:05.180 --> 07:06.510
Out of the question.

07:06.680 --> 07:08.640
We must win this race, Molly.

07:08.970 --> 07:11.510
Sir, the Arrow 2 is fast,
but not strong.

07:11.720 --> 07:14.390
-In order to win, we must...
-Trust the Nourasians? Never!

07:14.560 --> 07:17.520
Don't you see? They need this victory
as much as we do.

07:17.940 --> 07:19.520
But we can trust Aikka.

07:19.940 --> 07:23.530
You will neutralize the prince's mount
early in the race. That's an order.

07:23.690 --> 07:26.070
The Arrow 2 has been
newly equipped for the job.

07:30.370 --> 07:32.410
Trust me.
The pleasure will be all mine.

07:34.580 --> 07:37.580
This is exactly what the prince
has been ordered to do.

07:38.290 --> 07:39.170
What did you say?

07:39.540 --> 07:41.250
We don't want to fight him.

07:41.420 --> 07:44.010
His magic arrows
are very powerful.

07:45.920 --> 07:48.090
The heavy-duty cannons
are set, Mr. Wei.

07:48.260 --> 07:50.100
That's a job
well done, gentlemen.

07:50.260 --> 07:51.930
You can go to bed now.

07:52.140 --> 07:56.310
If he's as good as you say,
then we must strike first.

07:57.140 --> 07:58.980
Partner, you must be
really dreaming

07:59.150 --> 08:02.190
if you think your sweet prince
will keep his promise.

08:03.400 --> 08:05.070
If you can't trust
the Nourasians,

08:05.240 --> 08:07.240
at least you could trust me.

08:08.530 --> 08:11.410
I did trust you
during the last race.

08:11.570 --> 08:13.950
I won't make
the same mistake twice.

08:15.370 --> 08:16.660
You'll regret this!

08:20.540 --> 08:22.290
<i>And so will I.</i>

08:36.310 --> 08:37.230
Excuse me.

08:37.430 --> 08:38.810
Have you seen
this symbol before?

08:39.020 --> 08:41.190
It had something to do
with the crash on my star-racer.

08:41.980 --> 08:44.610
I'm asking everyone.

08:46.530 --> 08:48.400
Thanks.
I didn't think you would.

09:12.510 --> 09:14.350
This is... this is the place.

09:44.460 --> 09:47.590
What is this place,
some kind of twisted bad dream?

09:47.750 --> 09:49.010
Go away.

09:49.590 --> 09:51.720
Please, please...

09:51.930 --> 09:53.640
Let me live.

09:55.680 --> 09:57.850
I've come here
to talk to you, old man.

09:58.600 --> 10:00.350
I did exactly as you asked.

10:00.520 --> 10:02.730
Boom. The Earth racer.

10:03.650 --> 10:07.070
I put the explosives inside,
just as you commanded.

10:09.440 --> 10:11.280
You did what? Tell me!

10:11.440 --> 10:12.700
Who commanded you?

10:14.280 --> 10:16.320
You're not my master.

10:16.700 --> 10:18.080
Who is your master?

10:18.240 --> 10:19.910
Who ordered you to do this?

10:21.620 --> 10:23.290
The Timeless One.

10:31.260 --> 10:33.050
Who is The Timeless One?

10:33.300 --> 10:34.970
He's coming. Coming now.

10:35.180 --> 10:37.050
Who's coming? Tell me now.

10:43.180 --> 10:45.350
Hey, relax, old man.
What's wrong with you?

10:45.520 --> 10:47.270
I just want to talk with you.

10:50.610 --> 10:52.820
The Timeless One.
I don't get it.

10:52.990 --> 10:54.570
What is this madness?

11:11.090 --> 11:13.130
There goes all my evidence.

11:17.510 --> 11:18.600
Another one?

11:18.760 --> 11:20.260
Yeah, sure.

11:21.310 --> 11:24.350
And now
it's the Earth team...

11:25.940 --> 11:28.480
...against Prince Aikka of Nourasia.

11:29.860 --> 11:30.980
Go, Prince Aikka.

11:31.230 --> 11:33.360
Avenge us.
Beat the Earth team.

11:33.530 --> 11:35.530
Go, go.
Beat the Earth team.

11:43.450 --> 11:45.250
Jordan, please listen to me.

11:45.580 --> 11:47.420
If you hit the prince,
you'll hurt him.

11:47.580 --> 11:49.790
And if you miss him,
he'll probably hurt us.

11:49.960 --> 11:51.290
Is that really what you want?

11:54.460 --> 11:56.800
I'm just following orders,
Molly, like you should be.

11:57.050 --> 11:58.380
We don't need
to do this, Jordan.

11:58.550 --> 12:01.390
We can win this race
without using weapons.

12:01.600 --> 12:03.310
We're partners, remember.

12:04.180 --> 12:07.100
Sorry, but I took
the sucker punch in the last race.

12:07.270 --> 12:09.520
Crogs, one.
Earth team, zero.

12:09.690 --> 12:10.730
I'm sticking to the plan.

12:11.440 --> 12:12.570
Idiot.

12:13.730 --> 12:16.490
I'm tired of this frog prince.
He's going down.

12:27.790 --> 12:29.920
I beg you, sir.
We can't do this.

12:30.460 --> 12:32.670
We can do this and we will.

12:32.840 --> 12:36.210
Concentrate on the race, Molly.
And take him out early.

12:46.060 --> 12:47.980
<i>Molly, if you only knew</i>

12:48.180 --> 12:51.020
<i>how the future of our planet
hangs by a thread.</i>

12:51.190 --> 12:53.270
<i>We cannot afford another defeat.</i>

13:00.530 --> 13:02.570
Good night, sweet prince.
The sandman's coming.

13:23.720 --> 13:24.390
Gotcha!

13:32.150 --> 13:33.400
Molly, what are you doing?

13:33.560 --> 13:35.570
You're leaving us
totally unprotected.

13:40.740 --> 13:42.070
Hey, what's...

13:45.330 --> 13:47.160
Jordan, he's not gonna shoot.

13:51.210 --> 13:52.500
You locked me in here!

13:52.670 --> 13:55.290
Are you nuts?
Molly, let me out of here!

13:55.880 --> 13:57.710
Molly, what on earth
are you doing?

13:58.380 --> 14:01.260
I intend to win this race
the honorable way.

14:02.260 --> 14:03.890
Cockpit transmission off.

14:04.140 --> 14:05.800
Molly!

14:09.560 --> 14:12.640
Don Wei who was once
my father would understand.

14:12.810 --> 14:14.230
I'm sure he'd understand.

14:14.770 --> 14:17.690
Quickly, G'dar.
The Earth princess is on our tail.

14:22.360 --> 14:24.610
Prince Aikka, use your bow
as you were ordered.

14:48.550 --> 14:49.810
Nice move, princess.

15:07.280 --> 15:08.450
Nice move, Prince.

15:11.370 --> 15:13.700
Somebody get me out of here!

15:14.290 --> 15:16.250
-Any progress?
-Not yet, sir.

15:16.420 --> 15:19.040
The closing of the turret
is an emergency command.

15:19.210 --> 15:20.500
There's no outside override, sir.

15:21.920 --> 15:23.460
What can she be thinking?

15:26.510 --> 15:29.100
Sorry, Prince. I guess
I'm just too fast for you.

15:38.100 --> 15:39.900
UnsakaT <i>G'dar</i> wakhar!

15:51.740 --> 15:53.660
He's gaining on her.
What about the turret?

15:54.580 --> 15:55.790
We're in the security system.

15:56.620 --> 15:59.790
Try to open the turret doors
while I shut down Molly's access.

16:21.520 --> 16:24.730
Molly, could you keep your eyes
on the road and off the prince?

16:28.150 --> 16:30.200
Don't worry, Prince.
I'm right behind you.

16:31.160 --> 16:33.410
Jordan,
we're getting you out of there.

16:33.660 --> 16:34.830
You know what you have to do.

16:35.450 --> 16:36.450
Oh, boy. Do I!

16:46.550 --> 16:48.340
They've almost reached
the finish line.

16:48.510 --> 16:50.340
Are you sure
you want to do this, sir?

16:51.010 --> 16:53.760
We're going to win
this race my way.

16:54.180 --> 16:57.270
And we'll teach this mutineer
a lesson she'll never forget.

17:09.200 --> 17:10.570
I knew we'd win.

17:13.620 --> 17:14.620
Jordan, stop it!

17:19.540 --> 17:20.080
No!

17:25.210 --> 17:26.380
<i>Unsakafnourama barar!</i>

18:18.930 --> 18:22.060
I thought humans had honor,
but now I can see they have none.

18:23.140 --> 18:24.190
But I can explain...

18:28.940 --> 18:30.570
Prince Aikka, come back!

18:42.080 --> 18:42.660
Why?

18:43.080 --> 18:45.460
Why did you have
to ruin everything?

18:46.080 --> 18:48.710
You trusted the prince
more than me, partner.

18:49.670 --> 18:50.880
You idiot!

18:52.010 --> 18:52.800
Hey, don't push me.

18:54.550 --> 18:57.720
I trusted you,
and you let me down.

19:00.850 --> 19:01.930
Molly...

19:10.020 --> 19:12.940
All you had to do
was follow orders.

19:20.580 --> 19:23.080
I hope you're
pleased with yourself.

19:23.450 --> 19:25.540
Where do you think
you're going, young lady?

19:26.080 --> 19:28.790
Didn't your father
teach you any manners?

19:31.460 --> 19:32.800
No, he didn't.

19:32.960 --> 19:35.720
I'm going to my room,
and I'm never coming out.

19:36.800 --> 19:39.260
Do you think I'm going
to let you off that easily?

19:39.430 --> 19:41.260
Today was a sure win.

19:41.430 --> 19:44.390
We lost because
you didn't stick to the plan.

19:44.680 --> 19:46.520
Come back here, young lady!

19:46.690 --> 19:48.230
Do you hear me?

19:48.440 --> 19:49.900
Sir, calm down.

19:50.060 --> 19:52.320
You know, Molly really wanted
to win that race.

19:52.480 --> 19:54.530
So you're against me too, are you?

19:54.900 --> 19:57.570
-Is that it?
-Sir, of course not.

19:57.740 --> 19:59.570
Do any of you have any idea

19:59.910 --> 20:02.700
just how serious
my responsibilities are?

20:02.910 --> 20:04.370
Well, do you?

20:08.040 --> 20:09.670
I didn't think so.

20:21.100 --> 20:22.720
You know this symbol?

20:23.350 --> 20:25.680
You've probably never seen it,
don't want to help,

20:25.850 --> 20:26.980
got better things to do.

20:27.140 --> 20:28.940
You can just forget about it.

20:30.440 --> 20:32.230
I've never seen it before.

20:32.730 --> 20:33.570
I'm sorry, Rick.

20:41.910 --> 20:43.370
What do you want from me, Don?

20:44.490 --> 20:46.540
I just came down to say hello.

20:46.700 --> 20:48.210
What's wrong with that?

20:48.580 --> 20:50.170
Why do you think
I want something?

20:50.750 --> 20:54.500
Because the Earth team
just lost two races in a row.

20:55.380 --> 20:58.050
And because
I know you only too well.

21:07.430 --> 21:09.100
I'll have what my friend's having.

21:09.270 --> 21:10.940
Two "old fish soda" coming up.

21:15.230 --> 21:16.940
There you go, fellas.

21:20.570 --> 21:22.200
Well, bottoms up.
